  "_doc": "Shell commands and the action tokens every command classifier must give them: the proxy's actions.rs, @intutic/gate's actions.ts, intutic-clawde's gate/actions.py and the hook gates' hold classifier (gateBody.ts). Each implementation compares only the tokens it produces: the hold classifier knows deploy, publish, release and db_write (and, from gate v23, run_tests and the 3.1 tokens). notHeld commands classify to none of them. Every space in a pattern stands for whatever the shell or the database reads as a word break: SQL_GAP in actions.rs, the phrase matcher (shared-types phrases.ts, phrases.py) everywhere else. adversarial lists [unit, times] inputs every JavaScript and Python implementation must classify in under 200 ms: nothing may backtrack on them. 3.1 added migrate, prod_write, destroy, force_push and payment, emitted after the original eight in that order; DROP and TRUNCATE are both db_write and destroy; force_push is the git push phrase plus a whole-word --force or -f; rm -rf is destroy only when a target is absolute, starts with ~ or contains .. (Q3).",
